Frame: 800x540 CSS px at 2x = 1600x1080, 25 fps.
Smallest asserted text: 10.9 px in an 800 px embed.
Cue identifiers name the scene. A cue starts only after its scene's on-screen text was asserted.

boundary
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
The Fingerprint Lab opens with its limit: a statistical fingerprint, not a rating or a recommendation.

question
00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:12.480
The question: can 32 measurements from the first half-season find the same player in the second?

query
00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:18.840
Period A is the query: one player's first-half fingerprint, without the name.

reveal
00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:26.760
Against every eligible second-half profile, the fingerprint ranks him first. A role-and-minutes control ranks him 249th.

interval
00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:32.760
The 95% resampling interval, 1–43.5: how stable that rank is across observed matches. Not a forecast.

contributions
00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:40.320
What drove the match: each measurement's contribution, under learned weights fitted for 28 of the 32.

replay
00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:48.400
The Lab replays the stored result for every profile, beside a context-only control, each with its interval.

map
00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:54.880
The full map compares period A with period B across 32 features in 8 families.

caveats
00:00:55.360 --> 00:01:01.360
The caveats ship with the result. The strongest: same-season club continuity can make this test easier.

neighbors
00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:08.360
The nearest profiles in the same role, the query player excluded. Proximity is descriptive, not a recruitment recommendation.

comparison
00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:15.720
Each neighbor opens its evidence: the stored similarity, rebuilt family by family.
